      "text": "The course provides fundamental knowledge of single-variable and multivariable calculus: limits and continuity; derivatives and differentials; integrals, improper integrals, and their applications; partial derivatives, extrema, and several applied problems of multivariable functions; double integrals, triple integrals, line integrals of the first kind, line integrals of the second kind, and their applications to practical problems. The course trains students in problem-solving skills to deeply understand the theory and be creative in reasoning as well as proficient in calculation for practical requirements. Through this, the course provides future engineers, following the CDIO (Conceive - Design - Implement - Operate) standards, with logical thinking skills, a scientific approach, and the ability to use precise mathematical thinking to analyze problems in engineering practice.",
